   "id": 515424,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A chain of chicken restaurants offers a combo that includes your choice of 3 or 5 chicken strips, along with your choice of side dish. If there are 7 side dishes, how many different ways are there to build this combo meal?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The Multiplication Rule of Counting says that if there are <i>n</i> ways to accomplish one task and <i>m</i> ways to accomplish a second task, then there are <span data-math=\"n{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}m\"></span> ways to accomplish both tasks. You can tack on additional tasks by multiplying the number of ways to accomplish those tasks to your previous product.</p>\n<p>You have two choices of how many chicken strips you get (three or five).</p>\n<p>You have 7 choices of side dishes.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}7{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}14\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "14"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
